        defenseExam: [.direct("Did {D} swipe a transit card on the evening of the robbery?", "\"Yes. The card record shows a swipe on a bus at 9:50 p.m. that evening.\""), .direct("Where was the bus at that time?", "\"Two miles from the laundromat. That is a few minutes' drive at that hour.\""), .direct("Does the swipe prove where {D} was?", "\"It shows where the card was used. I cannot say whether {D} was holding it.\""), .direct("What is your role with the transit system?", "\"I supervise a group of bus routes and manage records of schedules and fare swipes.\""), .direct("How does a swipe get recorded?", "\"A rider taps a card, the reader logs the time and the vehicle, and the data uploads at the end of the night.\""), .direct("How accurate are those times?", "\"Within a minute or two. The reader clocks are synced daily with a central server.\""), .cross("What time did the robbery happen?", "\"Around closing, which is close to 10. I do not know the exact minute.\""), .cross("Could {D} have gotten off the bus and walked back?", "\"Two miles is a long walk, but it is possible. I would not rule it out.\""), .cross("Could the card have been used by someone else?", "\"Possible, but cards are registered to people, and most riders keep them on their person.\""), .cross("Does the record show where {D} got off?", "\"No. It records only the boarding swipe. There is no swipe for exit.\""), .cross("A swipe does not show who was holding the card, does it?", "\"Correct. It only shows that the card was used at that stop and time. I cannot tell you who tapped it.\"")],
