        theory: ("{D} burgled a funeral home.", "A passerby."),
        allocution: "\"I'm ashamed.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} pawned a ring the next day.", "The pry bar is a common brand."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why was your truck near the funeral home?", "\"I was passing through. It's on my way. I didn't stop there and I didn't go in.\""), .direct("Why did you have a pry bar in the truck?", "\"It's a work tool. Lots of people carry one. I use it for jobs, not for breaking into anything.\""), .direct("Did you take jewelry from the bodies?", "\"Never. That's a terrible thing. I'd never disturb the dead.\""), .direct("What do you do for work and why were you on that street?", "\"I work nights hauling for a landscape company. I was driving home on that street because it is the shortest way.\""), .direct("Did you stop near the funeral home?", "\"I pulled over for a few minutes to check a text. I did not get out of the truck or go near the building.\""), .direct("What about the ring you pawned?", "\"It was my own plain band. I needed cash for a bill, and I took it to the shop the next day.\""), .cross("The marks match your pry bar, don't they?", "\"That's what they say. It's a common tool. I don't know how it matches.\""), .cross("Your truck was near the lot at night, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I was driving by. I didn't know anything had happened.\""), .cross("A pry bar like yours made those marks. How is that not you?", "\"Because many people own that pry bar. I used mine for work and never touched that door.\""), .cross("You pawned a ring the day after the burglary. Doesn't the timing look suspicious?", "\"It looks that way. But the ring was mine, and I would not rob the dead.\""), .cross("You pawned a plain band the day after the burglary, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I pawned a ring of my own that I had owned for years. I needed rent money, and the shop keeps a record of it.\"")],
        openings: ("A funeral home's back door was pried and jewelry was taken from two bodies. A pry bar in {D}'s truck matches the marks, and {D}'s truck was near the lot. The State will show the tool marks, the inventory, and the street camera.", "The defense evidence includes a person passing through, a common work tool, and a ring that {D} says was {D.his} own. None of that makes {D} a burglar of the dead."),
        closings: ("A pried door, rings and a watch taken from the dead, and a pry bar from {D}'s truck that fits the marks. The truck was near the lot.", "A common pry bar and a truck on a public street. The State has not proved {D} entered the funeral home or took anything."),
        timeline: [(0, "1 a.m.: the truck."), (0, "1:15 a.m.: the door."), (0, "8 a.m.: the director finds it."), (1, "{DL} pawns a ring.")],
        identified: "Tool marks.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "They were their last keepsakes.",
        doctrines: ["searchSeizure"])

    static let bandRoomBurglary = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.bandRoomBurglary",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Thieves Take Band Instruments From High School", "Doors Left Unlocked After a Game"],
        law: "burglary2",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Broke and entered a building, a high school owned by {V}, with intent to commit larceny, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Fourteen instruments worth $22,000 were taken from a high school band room on {DATE}. A former band parent, {D}, had a key. {DL} says the key was lost.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Key Log", "A key issued to {D}."), E(.video, 2, "Hall Camera", "A figure with a cart."), E(.physical, 3, "Pawn Item", "A trumpet traced to {D}.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Lost Key", "{DL} says the key was lost.")],
        role: "Band director",
        exam: [.direct("What was taken from the band room on {DATE}?", "\"Fourteen instruments worth $22,000. I found the room emptied, and the whole program was thrown into chaos.\""), .direct("Who had a key?", "\"The key log shows a key issued to {D}, a former band parent. Few people had access.\""), .direct("What do the hall camera and pawn evidence show?", "\"A figure with a cart in the hall. A trumpet from our room was traced to {D} through a pawn record.\""), .direct("How did you find the burglary?", "\"At about 7 a.m. when I opened the band room. The shelves were bare. Fourteen instruments were gone, including trumpets, a clarinet, and a tuba.\""), .direct("How did you trace the key?", "\"I pulled the key log. Keys went to staff and several parents who helped with fundraisers, and one was issued to {D}.\""), .direct("What does the hall camera show?", "\"A figure pushing a cart out of the band room around midnight. The picture is grainy and shows no face.\""), .cross("{DL} says the key was lost, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I have no record of it being returned or reported.\""), .cross("Could someone else have used the key?", "\"Possibly. Keys get passed around. I can't say it's only {D}.\""), .cross("Can you identify the figure on the camera?", "\"No. The image is grainy. I can't say who it is.\""), .cross("How was the trumpet traced?", "\"A pawn shop reported a trumpet with our school's serial plate. The clerk gave deputies a slip with {D}'s name.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever return the key?", "\"I do not have a record that {D} did. I also have no record that {D} reported it lost.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Band parent",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How long did you work with {D} on band events?", "\"Several years. We ran concession stands together at football games and loaded buses for competitions.\""), .direct("What kind of parent was {D}?", "\"Generous with time. {D} stayed late to help students, brought food, and never asked for credit.\""), .direct("Did {D} ever talk about having keys?", "\"Once, {D} complained about a key ring being too heavy. That is the only time I remember keys coming up.\""), .direct("What did {D} say after the burglary?", "\"{D} said it was terrible and offered to help raise money for new instruments. That seemed sincere to me.\""), .direct("How was {D}'s relationship with the director?", "\"Friendly. They worked together on fundraisers, and I never heard a complaint.\""), .direct("Do you know whether {D} had money problems?", "\"I did not. {D} never mentioned any, and nothing I saw suggested it.\""), .cross("Did you know {D} had lost a key?", "\"I heard about it once, but I do not recall when. I cannot give you a date.\""), .cross("Do you know if {D} reported it?", "\"I do not. I never heard that {D} told the director.\""), .cross("Did you ever see {D} in the band room alone?", "\"No. Only at events with other parents.\""), .cross("Are you friends with {D}?", "\"Yes, and I know that makes me want to defend {D}. I am telling you what I have seen.\""), .cross("Were you at the school on the night of the burglary?", "\"No. I was home with my family and learned about it the next morning.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took instruments.", "A lost key."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} pawned the trumpet.", "The key was reported lost a month earlier."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the instruments?", "\"No. I never took anything from the school. I loved that band program. I volunteered for years.\""), .direct("What about the trumpet?", "\"I pawned a trumpet. I thought it was one we owned from my child's time in band. I never knew it was the school's.\""), .direct("How long were you involved with the band?", "\"Seven years. I chaperoned trips, ran concessions, and carried equipment for events. I loved watching the students perform.\""), .direct("What happened to your key?", "\"I lost it more than a month earlier, probably at a fundraiser. I looked for it and then forgot about it, and I should have reported it.\""), .direct("How did you come to have a key to the band room in the first place?", "\"I volunteered for three years as a band parent and was given a key to move equipment on game nights. Nobody asked me to turn it in after my child graduated.\""), .direct("When did you stop having the key, as far as you know?", "\"About a month before the break-in. I noticed it missing from my ring and told myself I would mention it, but I never did.\""), .cross("A trumpet from the band room was traced to you, wasn't it?", "\"That's what I hear. I'm shocked. I believed it was mine.\""), .cross("You had a key to the band room, didn't you?", "\"I did, once. I lost it. I don't know who found it.\""), .cross("Fourteen instruments is a lot, isn't it?", "\"It's a lot. I had nothing to do with it.\""), .cross("The trumpet had a school serial plate. How do you explain that?", "\"I never looked at the plate. I assumed it was mine, and I am embarrassed to say I was wrong.\""), .cross("You never told anyone you lost a key to the band room. Why not?", "\"I assumed I would find it. I should have said something to the director.\"")],
        openings: ("Fourteen instruments worth $22,000 were taken from a school band room. A key was issued to {D}, a former band parent, and a trumpet from the room was traced to {D} through a pawn record. The State will show the key log and the pawn item.", "The defense will point you to a key lost long before the burglary, a longtime band parent, and a trumpet {D} thought was {D.his} own. A lost key is not a burglary."),
        closings: ("Fourteen instruments gone, a key issued to {D}, and a band room trumpet in a pawn shop with {D}'s name. {D} had both the access and the proceeds.", "A lost key and a trumpet {D} thought was {D.his} own. The State has not proved {D} entered the band room or knew the trumpet was stolen."),
        timeline: [(-30, "The key is lost, {DL} says."), (0, "Midnight: the cart."), (0, "7 a.m.: the director."), (2, "The trumpet turns up.")],
        identified: "A key log.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "Students lost their season.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let churchOfficeSafe = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.churchOfficeSafe",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Thieves Cut Church Office Safe and Take Tithes", "Cutting Torch Used"],
        law: "burglary2",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Broke and entered a building, a church owned by {V}, with intent to commit larceny, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A church office safe was cut open with a torch on {DATE} and $12,000 in tithes taken. A torch tank belonging to {D}'s employer was missing. {DL} says it was lent.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Torch Tank", "Found in {D}'s garage.", .search), E(.forensic, 3, "Cut Marks", "Consistent with that torch."), E(.statement, 2, "Pastor", "The safe was cut Saturday night.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Lent", "{DL} says a friend borrowed the torch.")],
        role: "Pastor",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find at the church office on {DATE}?", "\"The office safe had been cut open with a torch sometime Saturday night, and $12,000 in tithes was gone. The cut was clean and deliberate.\""), .direct("What was found at {DL}'s home?", "\"A torch tank in {D}'s garage. It belongs to {D}'s employer and had been reported missing. The cut marks on our safe are consistent with that torch.\""), .direct("Why does that matter to you?", "\"Those tithes were given by members for the work of the church. Someone who knew how to use a torch took them, and the tank was in {D}'s possession.\""), .direct("How did you discover the safe had been opened?", "\"I came in Sunday at about 7 a.m. to prepare for service. The office door was shut, and the steel safe in the corner had a ragged hole cut near the lock.\""), .direct("What had been in the safe?", "\"About $12,000 in tithes and offerings collected over two Sundays, in envelopes waiting for the deposit. A few checks and the cash were taken.\""), .direct("What did the alarm record?", "\"The system was turned off at 11 p.m. Saturday with a valid code and turned back on a short time later. Nobody should have been in the building.\""), .cross("{DL} says the torch was lent to a friend, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A friend has also said so. I can't say who had the torch on Saturday night, only where it turned up.\""), .cross("Did you see anyone cut the safe?", "\"No. It happened overnight and I found it Sunday morning. I only know what the safe looked like and what deputies told me.\""), .cross("Are cut marks like these unique to one torch?", "\"Not unique. The report calls them consistent with that torch, which means it could have made them, not that no other torch could.\""), .cross("Who knew the alarm code?", "\"A handful of staff and volunteers, perhaps a dozen people. We changed it afterward.\""), .cross("Was {D} ever in the church office?", "\"Not that I know of. {D} was not a member of the staff, and I have no record of {D} coming in.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Friend who borrowed the torch",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you borrow {DL}'s torch?", "\"Yes. I asked to use it for a project, and {D} said yes without any fuss. We have known each other for years.\""), .direct("What did you use it for?", "\"I used it on a small welding job at my place. I kept it for a few days, then gave it back.\""), .direct("Did you ever tell {DL} what you planned?", "\"I mentioned a project but not the details. {D} didn't ask. It was a casual favor between friends.\""), .direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"We go back a long way and help each other with projects and trade tools back and forth.\""), .direct("What project did you use the torch for?", "\"A small welding job on a gate at my place. It took a day and a half, and I returned the torch and a small cylinder afterward.\""), .direct("When did you return it?", "\"Before the weekend of the burglary. I handed it back in the driveway and went home.\""), .cross("Did you have it on Saturday night?", "\"I had returned it by then, I believe. I'm not completely certain of the day, and I have no receipt.\""), .cross("Did you cut a safe with it?", "\"No. I used it on my own project and nothing else. I would never go near a church safe.\""), .cross("Did you ever visit that church?", "\"No. I have never been inside it. I have no connection to that church.\""), .cross("Can anyone confirm you returned the torch when you say?", "\"Not that I know of. It was just the two of us in the driveway.\""), .cross("You cannot say what the torch was used for after you returned it, can you?", "\"No. I handed it back at the shop and that was the last I saw of it. What happened afterward is not something I can speak to.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} cut a church safe.", "A lent torch."),
        allocution: "\"I'm so sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} knew the alarm code.", "The friend confirms he borrowed the torch."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why was your employer's torch tank in your garage?", "\"I'd brought it home from work for a weekend job. It was in my garage when deputies came, and I never hid it from anyone.\""), .direct("Did you lend it to anyone?", "\"Yes. A friend borrowed the torch the week before and returned it later. I lent it as a favor and did not ask what it was for.\""), .direct("Did you cut open the church safe?", "\"No. I have never been in that office. I was not involved in any theft from the church, and I'd never take tithes.\""), .direct("Why was your employer's torch tank at your house?", "\"I brought it home on a Friday for a weekend welding job and planned to return it Monday. It sat in the garage that week.\""), .direct("Who borrowed the torch?", "\"A friend asked to use it for a small repair. I lent it for a few days and got it back before the weekend.\""), .direct("Where were you Saturday night?", "\"At home, watching a game and going to bed early. I live alone, so nobody can back that up.\""), .cross("The torch tank was in your garage, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, it was. That looks bad, I know. But it was out of my hands for part of that week, and I didn't use it that night.\""), .cross("You cannot prove where you were Saturday night, can you?", "\"I was home, but nobody can confirm it. I live alone. I understand that is not much comfort to the jury.\""), .cross("Your employer reported that tank missing, didn't they?", "\"I understand they did. I had meant to return it Monday. I should have told them I took it home.\""), .cross("The torch matches the cut and was found in your garage. Why isn't that you?", "\"Because I lent it out, and anyone who had it could have used it. I never cut that safe.\""), .cross("You did not report the lending to your employer. Why?", "\"I did not think of it as a big deal. In hindsight, I should have asked before I brought the tank home.\"")],
        openings: ("A church office safe was cut open with a torch on a Saturday night and $12,000 in tithes was taken. A torch tank belonging to {D}'s employer was found in {D}'s garage, and the cut marks match. The State will show the tank and the marks.", "The defense will present a torch that was lent to a friend, marks that are only consistent with one tool of many, and nothing placing {D} at the church."),
        closings: ("$12,000 in tithes gone, a safe cut with a torch, and the missing torch tank sitting in {D}'s garage. The marks on that safe match that tank.", "A torch lent to a friend and marks that merely fit it. No witness, no video, and nothing that puts {D} in that office on Saturday night."),
        timeline: [(0, "Saturday 11 p.m.: the alarm off."), (0, "Sunday 7 a.m.: the pastor finds it."), (1, "The search."), (1, "{DL} is arrested.")],
        identified: "A torch tank.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .divided,
        impact: "Our offerings were gone.",
        doctrines: ["searchSeizure"])

    static let vanWithSleepingChild = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.vanWithSleepingChild",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Van Stolen With Sleeping Child Inside, Returned Unharmed", "Thief Abandons Van at Gas Station"],
        law: "felonyLarceny",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Took and carried away a motor vehicle valued over $1,000 belonging to {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A van with a sleeping four-year-old was stolen from a store lot on {DATE} and abandoned at a gas station thirty minutes later. The child was unharmed. {D} was filmed at the station. {DL} says {D.he} did not know the child was inside.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Station Camera", "{D} leaves the van."), E(.statement, 3, "Clerk", "'The child was asleep in the back.'"), E(.document, 2, "Keys", "Keys were in the ignition.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Unaware", "{DL} says {D.he} did not see the child.")],
        role: "Gas station clerk",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see at your station?", "\"A van pulled in and was left at a pump. The person who left it walked away fast. I found a four-year-old asleep in the back.\""), .direct("What does the station camera show?", "\"{D} leaving the van and walking off. The keys were in the ignition.\""), .direct("What was the child's condition?", "\"Asleep and unharmed, covered with a blanket. I called deputies right away.\""), .direct("What did you see at 3:30 p.m.?", "\"A white van pulled up fast and stopped crooked at pump four. A person got out, looked around, and walked toward the street without paying.\""), .direct("When did you notice the child?", "\"About five minutes later I heard crying from the van. I opened the sliding door and found a four-year-old strapped into a car seat under a blanket.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I called 911 and stayed with the child, talking calmly until deputies arrived. The child's parent got there about 3:45 and ran in crying.\""), .cross("Was the child hurt in any way?", "\"No. The child was fine. The child was only asleep.\""), .cross("Could {D} have seen the child?", "\"The child was covered by a blanket. It may have been hard to see from the front seat.\""), .cross("How long was the van at the station?", "\"I would estimate about thirty minutes. It was abandoned there.\""), .cross("Could the child be seen from the driver's seat?", "\"The seat was in the second row, and a blanket was draped over it. Someone sitting at the wheel might not have noticed.\""), .cross("Did the child say anything?", "\"Only that {V.he} wanted mommy. {V.He} was upset but not hurt, and I gave {V.him} a juice from the cooler.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Customer at station",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did {D} seem to know there was a child in the van?", "\"Not that I could tell. {D} got out and left quickly, and never looked toward the back of the van.\""), .direct("Why do you think {D} left so quickly?", "\"I do not know. {D} looked panicked, like something was wrong, and walked away without saying a word to anyone.\""), .direct("Did {D} say anything to you or to the clerk?", "\"No. {D} did not say a word to me. {D} just got out of the van and walked away.\""), .direct("What were you doing at the station?", "\"Filling up my car at the next pump. I saw the van pull in and stop suddenly.\""), .direct("What did {D} look like when getting out?", "\"Hurried and pale. {D} stared at the back of the van for a second and then took off on foot.\""), .direct("Did you hear anything from the van?", "\"Not until after {D} left. Then I heard a child crying, and the clerk came running.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} open the back of the van at any point?", "\"I did not see that. I only saw {D} get out of the front seat and leave.\""), .cross("How far were you from the van when this happened?", "\"About twenty feet. I could see {D} clearly, though not the inside of the van.\""), .cross("Did {D} look at the back seat before leaving?", "\"I could not tell. I did not see {D} look back there, but I was not watching closely.\""), .cross("Did {D} open the sliding door?", "\"No. I saw {D} open only the driver's door.\""), .cross("Did {D} say anything about a child?", "\"No. {D} did not say a word to anyone.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} stole a van with a child.", "Unaware."),
        allocution: "\"I'm so sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} left the child alone for thirty minutes.", "The child was covered by a blanket."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the van from the store lot?", "\"Yes, I did. The keys were in it, and I took it on impulse. It was a bad decision.\""), .direct("Did you know there was a child inside the van?", "\"No. I did not see a child. I never looked in the back, and the child was under a blanket.\""), .direct("What led you to take the van?", "\"I needed a ride across town and saw a van parked with the keys in the ignition. It was a quick, stupid impulse.\""), .direct("What did you do while driving?", "\"I drove straight to the station, and halfway there I heard a noise from the back. I assumed the van was making a sound and did not check.\""), .direct("Why did you leave the van at the station?", "\"The sound turned out to be crying. I panicked, left the van at the pump, and walked off. I thought someone would find the child quickly.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the back of the van when you first got in?", "\"It was dark in there and cluttered, with bags and a blanket over the rear seat. I did not stop and look closely, and I should have.\""), .cross("You never looked in the back seat, did you?", "\"No, I did not. I should have looked, and I will regret that for the rest of my life.\""), .cross("The child was left alone for about thirty minutes, wasn't the child?", "\"Yes. I did not know. I feel terrible about it, and I am very sorry.\""), .cross("You took a van that was not yours, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I did. I am so sorry. I did not think about who might be inside.\""), .cross("You heard crying and walked away from a child. How is that fear and not neglect?", "\"I was afraid of what I had done and not thinking. I should have gone back to the child at once.\""), .cross("Did you look into the back seat when you took the van?", "\"No. I did not look. I only saw the driver's seat and the keys.\"")],
        openings: ("A van with a sleeping four-year-old was stolen from a store lot and abandoned at a gas station thirty minutes later. {D} was filmed leaving it, and the child was unharmed.", "Listen for the defense evidence, which will show that {D} took the van but never saw the child under a blanket in the back, and left when crying frightened {D}."),
        closings: ("A stolen van, a child asleep in the back, thirty minutes alone, and {D} walking away. A person who takes a vehicle takes responsibility for who is in it.", "{D} did not see the child under a blanket and left when a cry frightened {D}. The State must prove {D} knew the child was there."),
        timeline: [(0, "3 p.m.: the van is taken."), (0, "3:30 p.m.: it is left at the station."), (0, "3:35 p.m.: the clerk hears crying."), (0, "3:45 p.m.: the mother arrives.")],
        identified: "A station camera.",
        aggravating: ["The victim was particularly vulnerable"],
        mood: .divided,
        impact: "I will never leave her again.",
        doctrines: ["mistakeOfFact"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let kayakLoadTheft = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.kayakLoadTheft",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Eighteen Rental Kayaks Taken From Lake Outfitter", "Trailer Backed Up at Night"],
        law: "felonyLarceny",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Took and carried away property valued at $19,000 belonging to {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Eighteen rental kayaks vanished from a lake outfitter on {DATE}. A camera showed a trailer. The trailer belonged to {D}. {DL} says {D.he} lent it.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Outfitter Camera", "A trailer with kayaks."), E(.document, 3, "Trailer Registration", "Registered to {D}."), E(.physical, 2, "Kayaks", "Eight found in {D}'s barn.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Lent", "{DL} says {D.he} lent the trailer.")],
        role: "Outfitter owner",
        exam: [.direct("What did you lose from your outfitter on {DATE}?", "\"Eighteen rental kayaks vanished overnight. They are my livelihood, and I had them ready for the weekend rentals.\""), .direct("What does your camera show?", "\"A trailer loaded with kayaks leaving the lot. The registration of that trailer comes back to {D}.\""), .direct("What was recovered?", "\"Eight of my kayaks were found in {D}'s barn when deputies searched. I identified them by the rental markings on the hulls.\""), .direct("How did you realize the kayaks were gone?", "\"At about 7 a.m. I opened the storage yard and found the racks empty and the gate chain cut. Eighteen rental kayaks were gone.\""), .direct("What did your camera capture?", "\"At about 2 a.m. a pickup pulled a flat trailer into the yard. Three people loaded kayaks quickly, and the trailer plate was visible.\""), .direct("How did deputies trace it?", "\"The plate came back to a registered trailer owned by {D}. They searched {D}'s barn and found eight of my kayaks with my labels.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} only lent the trailer, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I can't say who was towing it. The camera shows the trailer, not the driver's face.\""), .cross("Eight of eighteen were found. Where are the other ten?", "\"I don't know. They haven't turned up. That is part of why this has hurt my business so badly.\""), .cross("Are your kayaks the only ones of that kind around?", "\"No. They are a common model. What marks mine are the outfitter's labels, and those were on the ones in the barn.\""), .cross("Does the camera show the face of the person towing the trailer?", "\"No. The cab is dark and the camera only catches the trailer and the kayaks.\""), .cross("Did you find any of the others?", "\"No. Ten are still missing. I have seen listings for similar kayaks online but cannot say whose they are.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Cousin",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Do you know {DL}?", "\"Yes, we're cousins. I've known {D} my whole life. I visit the farm often and I know the barn.\""), .direct("Did you store kayaks in the barn?", "\"Yes. I helped move some in. They were stacked along one wall and I assumed they were part of something {D} was doing.\""), .direct("Did you know where they came from?", "\"No. Nobody told me. I didn't ask, and I didn't think anything was wrong.\""), .direct("How often are you at {D}'s farm?", "\"A few times a month. We are close, and I help with chores and visit family.\""), .direct("What did you see in the barn that day?", "\"Several kayaks stacked along one wall under a tarp. I helped move a couple closer to the door.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you about them?", "\"That a friend was storing them for a while. {D} did not seem worried.\""), .cross("Whose kayaks did you think they were?", "\"I assumed they were {D}'s, since they were in {D}'s barn. I didn't ask, and that was an assumption.\""), .cross("Did you notice any outfitter labels?", "\"Not that I remember. I wasn't looking at labels. I was moving boats.\""), .cross("Did you help load the trailer?", "\"No. I only helped carry them in the barn afterward. I wasn't there at the outfitter.\""), .cross("Did you look at the labels?", "\"No. I was only moving them. I did not think about where they came from.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} take the trailer out at night?", "\"No. I was not there and did not know about it until deputies came.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took kayaks.", "A lent trailer."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} sold two kayaks online.", "The kayaks in the barn were stored for a friend."),
        defendant: [.direct("Whose trailer is that on the camera?", "\"Mine. I lent it to someone for a few days. I didn't ask why, and I wasn't there when it was loaded.\""), .direct("How did kayaks end up in your barn?", "\"I let a person store some kayaks there. I didn't count them and I didn't look closely at where they came from.\""), .direct("Did you steal the kayaks?", "\"No. I did not take anything from the outfitter. I'm not a thief, and I would have told deputies who had the trailer.\""), .direct("How long have you owned the trailer?", "\"Five years. I use it to haul equipment and I lend it to friends when they need it.\""), .direct("Who borrowed it before the theft?", "\"Someone I know well. I do not want to name anyone without being certain. The trailer was out for a couple of days.\""), .direct("How did the kayaks get in your barn?", "\"Some were stored there as a favor. I did not count them and did not read the labels.\""), .cross("Eight stolen kayaks were in your barn, weren't they?", "\"Yes, they were. I can see why that looks bad. I was told they were being stored and I believed it.\""), .cross("You can't name the person who borrowed the trailer, can you?", "\"I know the person, but I don't want to name anyone without being sure. I realize that doesn't help me.\""), .cross("You didn't check the kayaks' markings, did you?", "\"No. I wish I had. The labels were probably right there, and I didn't look.\""), .cross("You allowed storage of a lot of boats without checking where they came from. Why?", "\"It was a favor, and I did not think to ask. That was a mistake.\""), .cross("Did you sell any kayaks online?", "\"I listed a couple for a friend. I did not realize any of them could be stolen.\"")],
        openings: ("Eighteen rental kayaks vanished from a lake outfitter. The camera shows a trailer registered to {D}, and eight of the kayaks were found in {D}'s barn. The State will show the video, the registration, and the recovered boats.", "The defense evidence includes a trailer that was lent out, kayaks stored in a barn without anyone checking their origin, and no camera view of who was driving."),
        closings: ("A trailer on the outfitter's camera registered to {D}, and eight of the missing kayaks in {D}'s barn. The trailer and the boats both lead to {D}.", "A lent trailer and a barn full of stored boats. The camera never shows {D}'s face, and the State has not proved {D} knew the kayaks were stolen."),
        timeline: [(0, "2 a.m.: the trailer."), (0, "7 a.m.: the owner."), (2, "Online listings."), (5, "The search.")],
        identified: "A registration.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["searchSeizure"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let busConverterRing = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.busConverterRing",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Catalytic Converters Cut From School Buses at District Depot", "Forty Buses Hit Overnight"],
        law: "felonyLarceny",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Took and carried away property valued at $38,000 belonging to {V}, a school district, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Converters were cut from twenty buses at a district depot on {DATE}. A cutting saw in {D}'s truck matched the cuts. {DL} says {D.he} is a mechanic.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Saw Marks", "Match {D}'s saw."), E(.video, 2, "Depot Camera", "A truck near the fence."), E(.document, 3, "Scrap Receipts", "Converters sold under {D}'s ID.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Mechanic", "{DL} says {D.he} is a mechanic.")],
        role: "District transportation director",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at your district depot on {DATE}?", "\"Catalytic converters were cut from twenty school buses overnight. The buses could not run until each was repaired, and it disrupted routes.\""), .direct("What tied {DL} to the cuts?", "\"A cutting saw in {D}'s truck matched the saw marks on the buses. A depot camera also shows a truck near the fence.\""), .direct("What do the scrap receipts show?", "\"Converters sold under {D}'s ID at a scrap yard. The yard recorded the sales and the identification used.\""), .direct("How did you discover the cut converters?", "\"Drivers found the buses not starting at 6 a.m., and a mechanic saw clean cuts where the converters had been. Twenty buses were affected.\""), .direct("What was the cost to the district?", "\"About $60,000 in replacement parts and repairs. Routes were delayed for several days, and some students waited in the cold.\""), .direct("What did the camera show near the fence?", "\"A dark pickup parked near the back fence just after midnight. It was too far away to read a plate.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} is a mechanic, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"But the saw marks match, and the scrap sales are in {D}'s name.\""), .cross("Can you see the truck's plate on the camera?", "\"Not clearly. The image shows a truck near the fence. I can't read a plate from it.\""), .cross("Do mechanics sometimes sell salvaged converters legally?", "\"Yes, I'm told so. Legitimate salvage is possible. I can only tell you that these were cut from our buses.\""), .cross("Did you recover any of the stolen converters?", "\"None from the depot. We learned a scrap yard bought converters from {D}, but I cannot say which ones came from our buses.\""), .cross("How many people have the same type of saw?", "\"It is a common brand. The examiner compared kerf and pattern and said it was consistent with {D}'s saw.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Scrap yard clerk",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Does {DL} sell to your scrap yard?", "\"Yes, regularly. {D} brings in converters and other salvaged parts, and we record the ID every time.\""), .direct("Does {DL} sell legally?", "\"As far as I know. {D} always has ID and paperwork. We have never had a problem with {D}.\""), .direct("What kind of seller is {DL}?", "\"Ordinary and straightforward. {D} doesn't try to hide anything and answers any question we ask.\""), .direct("What do you do at the scrap yard?", "\"I weigh incoming metal, record IDs, and pay sellers. I see a lot of mechanics bring in used parts.\""), .direct("What do you remember of {D}'s sales?", "\"{D} brought in converters in batches and always showed ID. Some looked fresh from a car, and others looked old.\""), .direct("What do you require for converters?", "\"ID, a signature, and a record of the date and weight. We do not ask where each one came from.\""), .cross("Do you check where converters come from?", "\"Not really. We check ID and weight. We have to trust what sellers tell us.\""), .cross("Can you tell a salvaged converter from a cut one?", "\"Sometimes by the cut ends, but I did not examine these closely. I couldn't say.\""), .cross("Did {DL} bring in a lot at once?", "\"Some weeks more than others. I don't have the exact numbers in my head.\""), .cross("Did {D} bring in converters from school buses?", "\"I do not know. We do not track the source of each one.\""), .cross("Did you notice anything odd about {D}'s sales that month?", "\"The count went up, but that is not unusual. A lot of shops sell more in certain seasons.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} stole converters.", "A mechanic."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} sold forty converters in a month.", "{DL} sells salvaged parts legally."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you have a cutting saw in your truck?", "\"I'm a mechanic. I use it every day on exhaust work. It's a tool of my trade, and I carry it wherever I work.\""), .direct("Where did the converters you sold come from?", "\"From salvage jobs. I sell parts I pull from scrapped vehicles. I use my own ID because I have nothing to hide.\""), .direct("Did you cut converters from the school buses?", "\"No. I have never been near that depot at night. I wouldn't touch school buses, because kids depend on them.\""), .direct("How long have you worked as a mechanic?", "\"Fourteen years. I repair exhaust systems, replace converters, and do salvage work on the side.\""), .direct("How do you get the converters you sell?", "\"From cars brought in for repair and from salvage vehicles. I remove the parts and sell them to the scrap yard with my ID.\""), .direct("How many converters did you sell that month?", "\"Many. I do high volume in the busy season. I keep invoices for each one.\""), .cross("The saw marks on the buses match your saw, don't they?", "\"That's what they say. Plenty of saws are the same brand. I can't explain how a match came out.\""), .cross("You sold converters under your own ID, didn't you?", "\"Yes, many times. It's legal for a mechanic. I never sold any I took from a school bus.\""), .cross("Your truck was seen near the fence, wasn't it?", "\"A truck was. Lots of trucks look alike. I don't know if it was mine, and I wasn't there that night.\""), .cross("Forty converters in a month is a lot. Where did they all come from?", "\"From repair jobs and from salvage cars that I bought. I can show invoices.\""), .cross("Your saw matches the cuts. Why should the jury discount that?", "\"Because many people have the same saw. It is the common tool for exhaust work.\"")],
        openings: ("Catalytic converters were cut from twenty school buses at a district depot. A cutting saw in {D}'s truck matches the marks, a truck was near the fence, and converters were sold under {D}'s ID. The State will show the saw, the camera, and the scrap receipts.", "The defense will point you to a mechanic who carries a saw and sells salvage legally under {D.his} own name, and a truck on a camera that nobody can identify."),
        closings: ("Twenty buses cut, a saw in {D}'s truck that matches the marks, and converters sold under {D}'s ID. Every road leads back to the same person.", "A mechanic owns a saw and sells salvage under a real name. The State cannot read the plate or show {D} at the depot, and that is reasonable doubt."),
        timeline: [(-30, "Sales begin."), (0, "Night: the cuts."), (0, "6 a.m.: drivers find them."), (5, "The search.")],
        identified: "Saw marks and receipts.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let truckStopRigTheft = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.truckStopRigTheft",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Semi Tractor and Trailer of Appliances Stolen From Truck Stop", "GPS Pings End at Scrapyard"],
        law: "felonyLarceny",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Took and carried away property valued at $168,000 belonging to {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A semi tractor and a trailer of appliances worth $168,000 were stolen on {DATE}. GPS tracked it to a lot leased by {D}. {DL} says {D.he} rented space and did not look inside.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "GPS", "The truck ends at {D}'s lot."), E(.document, 3, "Lease", "{D} leases the lot."), E(.physical, 2, "Trailer", "Appliance boxes in {D}'s shed.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Landlord", "{DL} says {D.he} only rented space.")],
        role: "Trucking company manager",
        exam: [.direct("What was taken from your company?", "\"A semi tractor and a trailer of appliances worth $168,000. The GPS tracked the rig to a lot.\""), .direct("Whose lot did the GPS lead to?", "\"A lot leased by {D}. The lease is in {D}'s name.\""), .direct("What did deputies find there?", "\"Appliance boxes in {D}'s shed. They matched our trailer's load.\""), .direct("How did you learn the rig was missing?", "\"The dispatcher called at 1:30 a.m. when the driver reported the rig gone from a rest stop. We tracked the GPS to a lot twenty miles away.\""), .direct("What was the load?", "\"A trailer full of new appliances: washers, dryers, and refrigerators worth $168,000. We hold the manifest and serial numbers.\""), .direct("What did deputies find at the lot?", "\"The tractor and trailer were parked in the back. The trailer was half empty, and appliance boxes were stacked in a shed on the property.\""), .cross("{D} says {D.he} only rented space, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D} said someone paid to park the rig and that {D} did not look inside.\""), .cross("Did anyone see {D} drive the rig?", "\"No. I have no witness who saw {D} at the wheel.\""), .cross("Were the appliances in {D}'s shed in the trailer?", "\"They were in a shed. We have not tied each box to the trailer yet.\""), .cross("Did {D} have any connection to your company?", "\"No. We have never done business with {D}, and I never heard of {D} before this.\""), .cross("Did the GPS tell you who was driving?", "\"No. It only shows where the truck went. It ends at {D}'s lot.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Truck stop attendant",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Who drove the rig into the lot?", "\"A person in a cap. I saw the rig come in and park, but I did not see the face clearly.\""), .direct("Was it {D}?", "\"Unclear. It could have been, but I did not get a good look.\""), .direct("How did the driver act?", "\"Calm. The driver parked and walked away. I thought nothing of it.\""), .direct("What do you do at the truck stop?", "\"I handle the fuel desk and parking lot. I see trucks come and go all night.\""), .direct("What did you see of the rig that night?", "\"A tractor and trailer pulled onto the lot next door at about 3 a.m. It parked in the back and the driver got out.\""), .direct("What did the driver look like?", "\"Average build, ball cap, and a jacket. I only saw the driver for a few seconds from across the road.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} that day?", "\"I saw {D} around the lot. I did not see {D} drive the rig.\""), .cross("Did {D} take cash from the driver?", "\"I do not know. I did not see money change hands.\""), .cross("How tall was the driver?", "\"Average. I really cannot say more.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} that night?", "\"I saw {D} on the property at another time, but I did not see {D} greet the driver.\""), .cross("Did you tell deputies you saw {D} drive?", "\"No. I told them I could not identify the driver.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} stole a rig.", "A landlord."),
        allocution: "\"I wish I hadn't.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} sold twelve appliances.", "A man paid {DL} to park it."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you steal the rig?", "\"No. I did not steal it. Someone paid me to park it on my lot.\""), .direct("Why was it on your lot?", "\"I rent out space. The person paid for space, and I did not look inside.\""), .direct("Did you sell any appliances?", "\"Some. I sold some that were in the shed. I did not know they were stolen.\""), .direct("What is your business?", "\"I own a gravel lot at the edge of town, and I rent space for equipment, trailers, and storage by the month.\""), .direct("Who paid you to park the rig?", "\"A person I met through a friend. It was a flat fee for a few days, paid in cash, and I did not ask about the load.\""), .direct("What did you do about the appliances in the shed?", "\"I sold some I thought were part of the arrangement. I did not know the load was stolen.\""), .cross("You sold twelve appliances from a stolen trailer, didn't you?", "\"I sold some. I thought they were part of the deal for parking.\""), .cross("You cannot give the person's name, can you?", "\"Only a nickname. I realize that leaves a hole in my story.\""), .cross("$168,000 in cargo sat on your lot. Did you not look?", "\"I did not. I should have. It was not my business, I thought.\""), .cross("You rented space to a stranger and sold goods from the trailer. How does that make you innocent?", "\"It does not make me wise. I trusted the person and I should have looked at what was in that trailer.\""), .cross("Why can you give only a nickname?", "\"Because that is all I was given. I did not take an ID, and I know that was foolish.\"")],
        openings: ("A semi tractor and a trailer of appliances worth $168,000 were stolen, and GPS tracked them to a lot leased by {D}. Appliance boxes were found in {D}'s shed, and twelve appliances were sold.", "Jurors will hear that someone paid {D} to park the rig, that {D} did not drive it, and that {D} did not know what was inside."),
        closings: ("GPS to {D}'s lot, appliance boxes in {D}'s shed, and twelve appliances sold. The rig was not parked by accident, and {D} knew what was inside it.", "A person in a cap drove the rig onto the lot, and no one saw {D} drive it. The State must prove that {D} knew the cargo was stolen, and it has not."),
        timeline: [(0, "1 a.m.: the rig is taken."), (0, "3 a.m.: it reaches the lot."), (1, "The company notices."), (2, "The search.")],
        identified: "GPS data.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let calfBarnTheft = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.calfBarnTheft",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Twelve Calves Stolen From Livestock Barn", "Hoofprints Lead to a Trailer"],
        law: "felonyLarceny",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Took and carried away livestock valued at $9,600 belonging to {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Twelve calves were taken from a livestock barn on {DATE}. Tire tracks matched a trailer owned by {D}. {DL} says {D.he} bought them at auction.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Tire Tracks", "Match {D}'s trailer."), E(.document, 3, "Brand Records", "Calves bore {V}'s brand."), E(.statement, 2, "Neighbor", "A trailer at 3 a.m.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 1, "Auction Receipt", "A receipt for calves.")],
        role: "Livestock owner",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at your livestock barn on {DATE}?", "\"Twelve calves were taken overnight. A neighbor saw a trailer at about 3 a.m., and I found the pen empty in the morning.\""), .direct("What tied {DL} to the theft?", "\"Tire tracks at the barn match a trailer owned by {D}. And the brand records show the calves bore my brand.\""), .direct("Why does the brand matter?", "\"Every calf of mine carries my registered brand. It is how I prove they are mine, and the records are filed with the state.\""), .direct("What did you discover that morning?", "\"At about 7 a.m. I found the barn gate open and twelve calves missing from the back pen. Hoof prints and tire marks led out toward the road.\""), .direct("How can you tell the calves were yours?", "\"Each calf carries my registered brand and an ear tag. Brand records show the calves taken bore my brand.\""), .direct("What did the neighbor report?", "\"A neighbor was up with a sick animal and saw a truck pulling a stock trailer along the road around 3 a.m. with its lights off.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} bought calves at auction, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A receipt exists for some calves. I can't say whether it covers mine.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} at your barn?", "\"No. I was asleep. I only know what the neighbor saw and what the tire tracks show.\""), .cross("Are your tire tracks unique to {DL}'s trailer?", "\"They match the trailer's tires. Lots of trailers share a tire type. It's a match, but I wouldn't call it a fingerprint.\""), .cross("Did the neighbor identify {D}?", "\"No. The neighbor described a truck and trailer but not a driver or a face.\""), .cross("Were any calves recovered?", "\"Two were found on {D}'s property with my brand. I do not know where the other ten went.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Auctioneer",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did {DL} buy calves at your auction?", "\"Yes. {D} is a regular buyer. I remember selling a few calves to {D} that season.\""), .direct("How is {DL} as a buyer?", "\"Honest and prompt. {D} pays the same day and has never given me any trouble.\""), .direct("Did {DL} get a receipt?", "\"Yes. Every buyer gets one. It lists what was sold and to whom.\""), .direct("What is your role at the auction?", "\"I am the auctioneer. I call the sale, sign the sale tickets, and make sure each lot matches the paperwork.\""), .direct("How does {D} shop at the auction?", "\"As a regular. {D} bids on a few calves, pays right away, and picks up the same day.\""), .direct("What did the receipt for {D} show?", "\"A few calves sold to {D} on a given date, with the lot numbers and prices.\""), .cross("Were the calves {DL} bought branded?", "\"Unclear. I don't recall for every lot. Some come in branded and some don't.\""), .cross("Did you sell calves from {V}'s herd?", "\"Not that I know. I sell many lots and I can't trace each calf's origin.\""), .cross("Can you say the receipt covers twelve calves?", "\"I'd have to check the receipt itself. I can't say from memory how many.\""), .cross("Were any of those calves branded?", "\"Some come branded and some do not. I do not remember each one.\""), .cross("Could you sell calves that had been stolen?", "\"It happens. We rely on sellers to be honest, and we check some papers, but not every calf.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} stole calves.", "An auction buy."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s receipt lists unbranded calves.", "The auction lot sold other calves that day."),
        defendant: [.direct("Where did you get the calves you had?", "\"At an auction. I bought calves there and hauled them home in my trailer. I have a receipt for what I bought.\""), .direct("Were you at {V}'s barn that night?", "\"No. I've never been to that barn. My trailer was used for hauling, and it's out on the road often.\""), .direct("Did you take twelve calves?", "\"No. I bought mine legitimately. I never saw a brand on any calf I bought, and I would not have taken stolen ones.\""), .direct("Tell the jury how you came to buy calves.", "\"I bought a few lots at the weekly auction. I loaded them on my trailer, brought them home, and kept them in a pen.\""), .direct("Did you check for brands?", "\"Not closely. The auction house gave me a receipt, and I trusted that. If any calf had a brand, I did not notice it in the pens.\""), .direct("Where was your trailer the night of the theft?", "\"In my yard, to my knowledge. I was asleep, and someone could have borrowed it.\""), .cross("The tire tracks match your trailer, don't they?", "\"That's what the deputies say. I can't explain it. My trailer goes lots of places.\""), .cross("Calves with {V}'s brand were found with you, weren't they?", "\"I was told that. I didn't notice any brand when I bought them. I'm surprised.\""), .cross("Your trailer was out at 3 a.m., wasn't it?", "\"I don't know where it was at that hour. I was asleep at home.\""), .cross("Your trailer's tire marks were at the barn and calves with {V}'s brand were with you. Why isn't that proof?", "\"It is circumstantial. Many trailers share those tires, and I did not take them.\""), .cross("The receipt lists unbranded calves. Doesn't that show these were different calves?", "\"It lists what the auction sold me. I cannot explain the branded ones, but they were not in that bill.\"")],
        openings: ("Twelve calves were taken from {V}'s livestock barn at about 3 a.m. Tire tracks match {D}'s trailer, and the calves bore {V}'s registered brand. The State will show the tracks, the brand records, and the neighbor's sighting.", "Jurors will also see an auction receipt for calves, an auctioneer who sold to {D}, and tire tracks that match thousands of trailers."),
        closings: ("A trailer at 3 a.m., tire tracks that match {D}'s trailer, and calves wearing {V}'s brand. The brand records settle whose animals they were.", "An auction receipt and a common tire. The State has not proved that the calves {D} had were {V}'s, or that {D} knew they were."),
        timeline: [(0, "3 a.m.: the trailer."), (0, "7 a.m.: the farmer finds the gate."), (2, "The brands are found."), (3, "{DL} is charged.")],
        identified: "Tire tracks.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["mistakeOfFact"])

    static let lumberLoadTheft = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.lumberLoadTheft",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Stacked Lumber Hauled Off From Building Site", "Flatbed Backs In After Dark"],
        law: "felonyLarceny",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Took and carried away property valued at $14,000 belonging to {V}, a builder, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Lumber worth $14,000 was taken from a building site on {DATE}. A flatbed was photographed. {D}'s flatbed had a matching dent. {DL} says {D.he} was hauling for a customer.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Site Camera", "A dented flatbed."), E(.document, 3, "Delivery Invoice", "{D} billed a customer for lumber."), E(.physical, 2, "Lumber Stamps", "Stamps match the site.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Customer", "{DL} says a customer hired {D.him}.")],
        role: "Builder",
        exam: [.direct("What was taken from your building site?", "\"Lumber worth $14,000. It disappeared from the site overnight, and a site camera photographed a flatbed.\""), .direct("What did the flatbed look like?", "\"It had a dent. {D}'s flatbed has a matching dent.\""), .direct("What links {D} to the lumber?", "\"{D} billed a customer for lumber with stamps that match my site. The stamps were found on the lumber.\""), .direct("How did you discover the missing lumber?", "\"I came to the site at 6 a.m. and found the framing stack gone. Stamps on the boards identified our supplier and the job lot.\""), .direct("What did the site camera show?", "\"At about 9 p.m. a flatbed with a dented fender pulled up. Midnight footage shows the truck leaving loaded with bundles of lumber.\""), .direct("What did {D}'s invoice show?", "\"{D} billed a customer for hauling and for lumber, with the same lot stamps as ours. That matches boards missing from my site.\""), .cross("{D} says {D.he} was hauling for a customer, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D} says a customer hired {D.him}. I cannot say the customer is not real.\""), .cross("Many flatbeds have dents, don't they?", "\"Many do. But this dent matches in several ways.\""), .cross("Did {D} bill the customer in cash?", "\"I understand so. That is what the invoice says.\""), .cross("Can you see {D}'s face on the video?", "\"No. The camera shows the truck and some figures at a distance. I cannot identify anyone.\""), .cross("Is the dent unique?", "\"It is distinctive, but dents on flatbeds are common. The deputies compared it to {D}'s truck and found a match.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Customer",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you hire {D} to haul lumber for you?", "\"Yes. I hired {D} to deliver a load of lumber to my project, and we agreed on a price.\""), .direct("Did you believe the lumber was meant for your job?", "\"I thought so. {D} told me it was a load I had ordered, and I had no reason to doubt it.\""), .direct("How did you pay {D} for the delivery?", "\"In cash. That is how we agreed. I have a record of the payment in my phone.\""), .direct("How did you come to hire {D}?", "\"A friend recommended {D} for hauling. I needed a load of lumber moved to my project and agreed to a price.\""), .direct("How was the delivery arranged?", "\"{D} said the lumber would be ready late in the day and brought it to my place after midnight. I paid on delivery.\""), .direct("Why did you pay in cash?", "\"{D} asked for cash and I had it on hand. We had a handshake agreement and a note on a pad.\""), .cross("Did you check where the lumber came from before paying?", "\"No. I did not check. I trusted {D}, and I did not look at the stamps on the boards.\""), .cross("Did you know the lumber was stolen from a building site?", "\"No. I had no idea. If I had known, I would not have accepted the delivery.\""), .cross("Are you related to {D} or close to {D}?", "\"No. I am only a customer. I hired {D} for hauling and nothing more.\""), .cross("Did you ask where the lumber had been before?", "\"No. I assumed it came from a yard. I did not ask.\""), .cross("Did you notice the stamps on the boards?", "\"I saw writing on the boards but did not read it. I know now that it was our builder's lot code.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took lumber.", "A hauler."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} billed the customer in cash.", "The customer is a real name in {DL}'s phone."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you steal the lumber from the building site?", "\"No. I hauled lumber for a customer. I did not take it from any site, and I did not know it was stolen.\""), .direct("Who was the customer who hired you?", "\"A customer I know. The name is in my phone, and the customer paid me in cash for the haul.\""), .direct("Why did you take cash for the job?", "\"The customer asked for cash. I did not think twice about it, because many of my customers pay that way.\""), .direct("What is your hauling business?", "\"I own a flatbed and haul materials for builders and homeowners. I get jobs by word of mouth and quote them by the load.\""), .direct("How did you get this job?", "\"A customer called and said there was a load of lumber to move from a lot to a project. I agreed and picked it up that night.\""), .direct("What did you do when you were told it was stolen?", "\"I was shocked. I showed the deputies the customer's name in my phone and told them how I was paid.\""), .cross("The lumber stamps match the building site, don't they?", "\"They do. I did not look at the stamps. I just delivered what I was asked to deliver.\""), .cross("Your flatbed matches the dent on the site camera, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. It is my truck. I was working that night, and I did go past that area.\""), .cross("You billed in cash for lumber that turned out to be stolen. How do you explain that?", "\"I thought the job was legitimate. I did not know where the lumber came from.\""), .cross("You drove to a building site at night, loaded lumber, and left. Isn't that how a thief works?", "\"It is also how a hauler works when the customer says it is easiest at night. I thought it was legitimate.\""), .cross("The lumber had the site's own stamps. You didn't notice?", "\"I saw stamps but did not read them. Lumber has stamps on it everywhere.\"")],
        openings: ("Lumber worth $14,000 was taken from a building site, and a camera photographed a dented flatbed. {D}'s flatbed has a matching dent, and {D} billed a customer for lumber with the site's stamps.", "By the end of this trial, the proof will show that {D} was hired to haul lumber for a customer who is a real person and that {D} never knew it was stolen."),
        closings: ("A dented flatbed on camera, lumber with the site's own stamps, and an invoice in {D}'s name. These pieces match one another too well to be a coincidence.", "A hauler who delivered lumber for a customer and was paid in cash. The State must prove {D} knew it was stolen, and a delivery job is not a theft."),
